<title>SPAIN: SWIMMING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the third day of the</p>
<p>European Swimming Championships on Friday:</p>
<p>Women's 25 kilometres</p>
<p>1. Rita Kovacs (Hungary)  Five hours 21 minutes 58 seconds</p>
<p>2. Valeria Casprini (Italy) 5:23:28 </p>
<p>3. Edith Van Dijk (Netherlands) 5:25:28 </p>
<p>4. Peggy Buchse (Germany) 5:30:15</p>
<p>5. Etta Van De Weijden (Netherlands) 5:31:26</p>
<p>6. Radka Nechmakova (Czech Republic) 5:33:52</p>
<p>7. Gaia Naldini (Italy) 5:39:10</p>
<p>8. Attilia Figini (Switzerland) 5:39.27</p>
<p>9. Susanna Quaglierini (Italy) 5:42:36</p>
<p>10. Annette Andermatt (Switzerland) 5:43.28</p>
<p>11. Severine Leroy (France) 5:49:32</p>
<p>12. Britta Kamrau (Germany) 5:53:03</p>
<p>13. Eva Novakova ((Czech Republic) 6:05:02</p>
<p>14. Vanessa Bouisset (France) 6:09:31</p>
<p>Did not finish:  Alix Scott (Britian), Sara-Louise Ward</p>
<p>(Britain)</p>
